1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,765
That was the best night of my life.

2
00:00:14,365 --> 00:00:16,268
It was also the night my dad lost his job.

3
00:00:22,068 --> 00:00:27,710
Quân, I'm at the school gate. Text me when you're done, I'll pick you up.

4
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:33,795
This song...

5
00:00:38,795 --> 00:00:43,984
Twelve hours earlier, things at home were normal. At least, I thought so.

6
00:00:45,784 --> 00:00:47,883
You're not finishing that egg, right, Dad?

7
00:00:48,183 --> 00:00:48,700
Go ahead.

8
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,224
A white shirt? It's not even Monday.

9
00:00:53,524 --> 00:00:54,533
Yeah. There's a meeting.

10
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,388
What meeting needs you dressed up?

11
00:00:56,688 --> 00:00:57,815
An... important one.

12
00:00:58,615 --> 00:01:00,110
Got your mock exam scores yet?

13
00:01:00,410 --> 00:01:01,620
Yep. Four and a half.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:06,389
Four and a half?! And you can still eat like that?

15
00:01:06,689 --> 00:01:08,747
Eating less won't raise my score, Mom.

16
00:01:09,047 --> 00:01:13,520
Four and a half and you're joking? You think life is easy?

17
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:15,014
Hey...

18
00:01:15,614 --> 00:01:19,520
The exam's ages away. You act like the world's ending.

19
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:22,038
I've got group study tonight. Don't wait for me.

20
00:01:23,038 --> 00:01:30,481
Dad had never yelled at me about grades. That day I just thought he was being unfair. Nobody noticed the shirt.

21
00:01:31,081 --> 00:01:32,688
There was no study group.

22
00:01:35,688 --> 00:01:39,936
Hey, look! A city-wide band competition. The final's on TV.

23
00:01:40,236 --> 00:01:40,933
How much to enter?

24
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:44,055
Three million a band. I can cover it.

25
00:01:44,355 --> 00:01:46,762
Tùng said 'three million' like it was three pieces of candy.

26
00:01:47,062 --> 00:01:50,096
Nah, split it three ways. I'll cover mine.

27
00:01:50,396 --> 00:01:54,098
So what do we play? Covers won't get us far.

28
00:01:55,898 --> 00:02:01,099
I've got one. Dug it out of our storage room. Guaranteed nobody's heard it.

29
00:02:01,399 --> 00:02:07,260
The notebook was at the bottom of a box labeled 'Dad's old stuff.' I only read the word 'old.'

30
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,362
Who wrote it?

31
00:02:08,662 --> 00:02:14,383
No idea. Just an H. and 1999. Some old guy, probably.

32
00:02:15,183 --> 00:02:18,171
A song that sad? Who'd listen? Competitions need energy.

33
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:22,326
Every band will bring energy. Sad is what people remember.

34
00:02:22,626 --> 00:02:23,757
Two votes to one.

35
00:02:24,057 --> 00:02:26,126
If this is democracy, why am I paying?

36
00:02:28,926 --> 00:02:31,293
At the same time, across the city.

37
00:02:31,793 --> 00:02:35,553
Hải... I'm sorry. The machines do all the testing now.

38
00:02:35,853 --> 00:02:39,052
It's fine. It's not your fault.

39
00:02:43,252 --> 00:02:45,141
Want me to refer you somewhere?

40
00:02:45,441 --> 00:02:48,351
At my age, they'd rather hire a machine.

41
00:02:49,151 --> 00:02:53,710
The worse things got, the more Dad joked. I got that from him.

42
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:55,982
Eleven years... fits in one box.

43
00:03:04,982 --> 00:03:06,137
This song... it's really sad.

44
00:03:06,437 --> 00:03:07,220
Sad is good.

45
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,574
You skipped lunch?

46
00:03:09,874 --> 00:03:10,487
I forgot.

47
00:03:10,787 --> 00:03:13,856
Here, take my bánh mì. I ate at home.

48
00:03:14,156 --> 00:03:18,144
I hadn't eaten. But a lead singer has to look the part.

49
00:03:21,444 --> 00:03:26,676
Lan, I'll be straight with you. This year the school is ordering from a company.

50
00:03:26,976 --> 00:03:28,544
All three hundred sets?

51
00:03:28,844 --> 00:03:32,688
Yes. They're cheaper. It wasn't my call.

52
00:03:32,988 --> 00:03:37,887
What if I take ten percent off? My work's always better made.

53
00:03:38,187 --> 00:03:41,429
I know that. But they're giving twenty off.

54
00:03:42,229 --> 00:03:43,670
Okay. I understand.

55
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:49,897
Three hundred sets... that's two months of interest.

56
00:03:53,697 --> 00:03:54,809
Pick up...

57
00:03:55,809 --> 00:04:00,493
At six, I texted Mom. She replied in four seconds.

58
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:06,809
My dad already booked dinner to celebrate. Win or lose.

59
00:04:07,109 --> 00:04:08,995
My parents don't even know I'm here.

60
00:04:10,395 --> 00:04:10,885
Oh no.

61
00:04:11,185 --> 00:04:11,496
What?

62
00:04:11,796 --> 00:04:14,009
My mom wants to bring dinner to... somebody's house.

63
00:04:14,309 --> 00:04:17,978
Say it's mine. I live way out in Gia Lâm, she won't come.

64
00:04:22,578 --> 00:04:22,845
Saved.

65
00:04:26,845 --> 00:04:27,688
That's fine too.

66
00:04:29,188 --> 00:04:33,437
Barely off the hook and already laughing. You never worry about anything, do you?

67
00:04:33,737 --> 00:04:36,852
Why worry? Everything sorts itself out.

68
00:04:37,352 --> 00:04:38,000
Must be nice.

69
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,553
I have to leave right after we play.

70
00:04:40,853 --> 00:04:41,726
We're up!

71
00:04:57,026 --> 00:05:03,382
At the chorus, I closed my eyes. There was one note I always sang off key, and that night I missed it right on cue.

72
00:05:18,982 --> 00:05:20,554
Wrong note, son...

73
00:05:22,054 --> 00:05:25,097
At eighteen, I stood right there too.

74
00:05:30,597 --> 00:05:31,613
That was amazing, man!

75
00:05:34,913 --> 00:05:37,265
Mai! Stay and celebrate!

76
00:05:37,565 --> 00:05:40,199
I've got a shift. I'm late.

77
00:05:40,499 --> 00:05:41,177
A shift? For what?

78
00:05:41,477 --> 00:05:42,751
Later. I'll tell you tomorrow.

79
00:05:46,551 --> 00:05:49,339
Mom told me this part much, much later.

80
00:05:50,139 --> 00:05:51,489
Why didn't you pick up?

81
00:05:52,989 --> 00:05:53,809
I'm done there.

82
00:05:54,109 --> 00:05:55,099
Done... what do you mean?

83
00:05:55,399 --> 00:06:00,742
They cut the whole testing team. Machines are faster. Cheaper.

84
00:06:05,742 --> 00:06:07,715
The school canceled its uniform order today, too.

85
00:06:09,715 --> 00:06:10,701
The fifteenth...

86
00:06:11,001 --> 00:06:11,515
I know.

87
00:06:12,515 --> 00:06:16,222
I can cover half this month. The other half...

88
00:06:16,722 --> 00:06:18,101
I've still got a little saved.

89
00:06:18,401 --> 00:06:20,089
That's his university money.

90
00:06:20,389 --> 00:06:21,538
We'll deal with that later!

91
00:06:23,038 --> 00:06:24,389
Why are you yelling at me?

92
00:06:24,889 --> 00:06:27,318
I told you back then not to borrow to expand the shop.

93
00:06:27,818 --> 00:06:30,919
Back then you also said nobody at your company could replace you.

94
00:06:34,919 --> 00:06:38,151
Don't tell him. His exams are coming.

95
00:06:38,951 --> 00:06:41,076
He's not at group study, you know.

96
00:06:41,376 --> 00:06:42,175
How do you know?

97
00:06:43,375 --> 00:06:46,271
...Just a guess. Go to sleep.

98
00:06:50,271 --> 00:06:53,081
I'm home! Group study was exhausting.

99
00:06:53,381 --> 00:06:54,455
Have you eaten?

100
00:06:54,755 --> 00:06:55,941
I ate with friends.

101
00:06:57,441 --> 00:06:59,418
Group study... and you bring a guitar home?

102
00:06:59,718 --> 00:07:00,959
Oh... a friend asked me to hold it.

103
00:07:01,959 --> 00:07:02,254
Okay.

104
00:07:03,054 --> 00:07:06,711
Dad just said 'okay.' Back then I thought I'd gotten away with it.

105
00:07:07,211 --> 00:07:10,873
Go shower. You've got school tomorrow.

106
00:07:21,373 --> 00:07:22,723
What's that you're humming?

107
00:07:23,023 --> 00:07:23,988
Just an old song.

108
00:07:29,988 --> 00:07:32,143
I thought Mai was the only one who caught that note.

109
00:07:34,443 --> 00:07:38,396
At that same moment, in my parents' room, another phone lit up.

110
00:07:38,996 --> 00:07:43,369
One asked for a million. The other asked for a lot more.

111
00:07:48,069 --> 00:07:48,793
...Streetlights.

112
00:07:56,793 --> 00:07:59,034
Mom, I need a million for study materials.

113
00:07:59,334 --> 00:08:01,082
Where did the money in the envelope go?

114
00:08:01,382 --> 00:08:03,760
You're not worried? Seriously?

